# What playing each class feels like at its level: styles and spells in general terms, pets for pet
# classes, heals for healers, stealth for stealthers, solo and group life, gear and spec musings, class
# pride, class envy and jokes about one's own class. Classic and Shrouded Isles classes only, each in its
# own realm. Role lines at the end. Adds to classes.lines and classes_more.lines. New writing (see docs/bot-voices).

# ======================================================================== Albion
@kind ambient
@topic class
@realm alb

# ---- Armsman
@class Armsman
@levels 1-19
[at this level|this early] my armsman has like three styles and i [mash|spam] all of them
getting the first real set of plate is a big day for an armsman
an armsman at this level is mostly a tin can with a sword
@levels 20-34
[polearm|two handed] armsman [life|here], [slow|big] swings and [even bigger|bigger] [hits|numbers]
guarding the cleric is half my job and the half i take most seriously
i see a paladin chanting and wonder what it is like to bring more than a sword
crossbow on an armsman is for pulling and nothing else, and it does that fine
@levels 35-50
at this level an armsman is mostly a [wall|door|shield] with [opinions|feelings|a polearm]
parry, shield and plate. some fights i dont even notice the add hitting me
more polearm or more shield, every respec i [end up back where i started|flip the other way|talk myself out of it]
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
the armsman way: [taunt|hit] it, [stand there|stay put], [trust the healer|hope the healer is awake]
@invites boast
no class takes a beating like an armsman and i will hear no argument
@invites
soloing on an armsman is slow but steady, plate forgives a lot
@who Crafter
an armsman's repair bill could feed a small village
@who

# ---- Paladin
@class Paladin
@levels 1-19
[early on|at these levels] a paladin is just a tank who [hums a lot|sings under their breath|never stops chanting]
one chant at a time for now, twisting can wait
@levels 20-34
chant twisting [finally|almost] makes sense, [my fingers hurt|my hotbar is a mess|my keyboard hates me]
paladin in a group: chants up, taunt up, nobody thanks the chants
the endurance chant is why the whole group can keep swinging
@levels 35-50
[twisting four chants|keeping four chants going] and [still swinging|still taunting] [feels like juggling|is a full time job]
two handed paladin damage is better than people say. not great, but better
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
paladins dont run out of endurance, we [hand it out|sing it to everyone|share it around]
plate, a big sword and a choir of chants. the paladin dress code
@invites
[i love my chants|chants are great] but some days i envy the armsman [polearm|damage|hits]
@invites boast
a group with a paladin just lasts longer, endurance and health regen add up
@invites complaint
solo paladin is slow, chants cant kill things for you

# ---- Mercenary
@class Mercenary
@levels 1-19
dual wield at this level [misses a lot|feels clumsy], but when both swings land [it is great|it is lovely|wow]
starting merc, still figuring out which hand does what
@levels 20-34
evade and parry stacking on my merc, half the hits just go past me now
merc solo is a gamble, sometimes the yellow dies, sometimes i do
chain armor and two swords, the merc uniform
@levels 35-50
[at this point|this far in] a merc in chain [does more damage than|outdamages] half the [realm|tanks i know]
two weapons, no shield, no apologies
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
[the class is called mercenary|i am a mercenary] but [nobody ever pays me|the pay is terrible|the coin all goes to repairs]
@invites
merc envy is real, i look at reaver lifetaps every time i get low
@invites boast
nothing beats watching both hands crit at once on a merc
@invites
a merc in a group just needs a target and a healer who likes them

# ---- Reaver
@class Reaver
@levels 1-19
a young reaver is just a [fighter|merc] with a flail and [dreams|big plans]
low level reaver, the flex skill is still pretty sad
@levels 20-34
[soulrending|my] lifetaps keep me going when the healer [runs dry|goes oom|looks away]
the pbaoe on a reaver makes every pull a little exciting
reaver in a group means the healer has one less person to worry about
@levels 35-50
high level reaver: [lifetap|tap], [pulse|swing], [smile|grin]
the flex reach on a reaver still feels like cheating
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
reavers [look evil|look scary] but [we|most of us] just want [a group|to be invited|someone to talk to]
@invites
i see paladins get groups and remind myself reavers exist too
reaver solo is underrated, the lifetaps make up for no healer
@invites boast
black chain and a spiked flail, the reaver look is unmatched

# ---- Scout
@class Scout
@levels 1-19
early scout is all [missing|hoping], the bow spec [comes later|grows on you]
first time something walked right past me while i was hidden, scouts are fun
@levels 20-34
scout solo: [draw|shoot], [release|shoot again], [hope|pray] it [dies|falls] before it [arrives|reaches me]
hidden on a hill with a longbow, waiting. that is the scout life
@levels 35-50
a scout with a [good|decent] bow and high bow spec is a [scary|frightening] thing
a shield on a scout really saves lives, mine mostly
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
scouts always get to the loot last, we stand so far back
@invites
scout envy: watching an infil walk up and stab things without a worry
[a scout in a group|in a group a scout] [pulls|pulls everything], [shoots|plinks] and [stays out of the way|tries not to die]
@invites boast
albion archery is the best in the land, i will say that to any hunter or ranger
@invites complaint
arrows cost money, nobody tells you that when you roll a scout

# ---- Infiltrator
@class Infiltrator
@levels 1-19
low level infil, [mostly|] [stealthing|sneaking] past things i cant kill yet
@levels 20-34
applying poisons before every fight, the infil ritual
backstab, [follow up|chain], [vanish|gone], [the infil way|that is the job]
infil solo at this level is slow and careful, and i like careful
@levels 35-50
[this high|at this level] an infil is [mostly|all] [patience|waiting] and [one|a single] [great|perfect] moment
high crit strike on an infil, one good opener ends most fights
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
infils dont lose fights, we just [never start|walk away from|quietly leave] the ones we would lose
@invites
minstrels stealth too and still get invited, infil envy is real
nobody asks for an infil in a pve group and i dont blame them
leather and two short blades, light and quick
@invites boast
nobody in albion moves quieter than an infil, that is a fact

# ---- Minstrel
@class Minstrel
@levels 1-19
minstrel at this level: [one song|a few songs] and a lot of [hope|enthusiasm]
@levels 20-34
[my charmed pet|the charm] broke [again|mid fight], [minstrel problems|that is minstrel life]
[speed song and power song|power song and speed song] [twisting|swapping], [the|my] group [never|hardly] [notices|thanks me]
mez on a minstrel is the most useful thing i do and nobody sees it
@levels 35-50
high level minstrel [is|feels like] half [tank|fighter] half [jukebox|music box]
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
they call minstrels the realm's radio and i am fine with it
@invites
minstrels have stealth too, people forget that
i do envy bards a little, they get heals with their songs
chain armor and a lute, the minstrel is better armored than people think
@invites boast
speed to the frontier, courtesy of your local minstrel

# ---- Cleric
@class Cleric
@levels 1-19
low level cleric, [mostly smite|smiting things] until [someone needs|the group needs] me
the first rez on a cleric is a big moment, i still remember mine
@levels 20-34
rejuv cleric [in a group|with a full group], [eyes on|watching] the health bars the whole time
a cleric's buffs are half the reason the tank lives, nobody says it
@levels 35-50
[high level|veteran] cleric means rezzing [the same|one] person [three|four] times a night
smite spec at this level is serious damage, nobody believes it until they see it
@levels 1-50
@invites joke
[the tank dies|the puller dies|someone dies], the cleric gets [blamed|the tell]
@invites
clerics in chain, wizards in robes, i know who got the better deal
solo cleric is slow but i can heal myself through anything
@invites boast
albion clerics, holding up every group in the realm
@who Socialite
@invites
half my friends list is people i rezzed once
@who

# ---- Friar
@class Friar
@levels 1-19
friar at this level is just a monk with a stick
@levels 20-34
